# Returns Query API

## Overview

The returns query endpoint provides flexible querying of return records with support for filtering, searching, pagination, sorting, and relation expansion.

**Endpoint:** `POST /server/return/query`

## Request Parameters

### Pagination & Sorting

| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
|-----------|------|---------|-------------|
| `page` | integer | 1 | Page number |
| `limit` | integer | 20 | Items per page |
| `orderBy` | string | created_at | Field to sort by |
| `ascending` | boolean | false | Sort direction (true = ascending, false = descending) |

### Search

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `search` | string | Multi-field search across return number, customer name, order number, tracking number, and notes |

### Expansion

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `expand` | string | Comma-separated relations to expand (customer, order, fulfillment, location, items, items.variant, items.order_item) |

### Filters

#### Basic Filters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `status` | string | Filter by status (REQUESTED, APPROVED, IN_TRANSIT, RECEIVED, INSPECTED, COMPLETED, REJECTED, CANCELLED) |
| `type` | string | Filter by type (RETURN, EXCHANGE) |
| `reason` | string | Filter by reason (DEFECTIVE, SIZE_FIT, WRONG_ITEM, NOT_AS_DESCRIBED, CHANGED_MIND, OTHER) |
| `resolution` | string | Filter by resolution (REFUND, EXCHANGE, STORE_CREDIT) |
| `customer` | uuid | Filter by customer UUID |
| `order` | uuid | Filter by order UUID |
| `fulfillment` | uuid | Filter by fulfillment UUID |
| `location` | uuid | Filter by location UUID |
| `refund_processed` | boolean | Filter by refund processing status |

#### Date Range Filters

| Parameter | Type | Description |
|-----------|------|-------------|
| `requested_after` | ISO date | Returns requested after this date |
| `requested_before` | ISO date | Returns requested before this date |
| `completed_after` | ISO date | Returns completed after this date |
| `completed_before` | ISO date | Returns completed before this date |
| `created_at_from` | string | Filter returns created on or after this date (YYYY-MM-DD) |
| `created_at_to` | string | Filter returns created on or before this date (YYYY-MM-DD) |

## Available Expansions

### `customer`
Expands the customer relation to include full customer details:
- Basic info (id, eid, xid, first_name, last_name, email, phone)
- Address information
- Customer settings

### `order`
Expands the order relation to include order details:
- Order number, status, totals
- Order dates and metadata
- Payment and shipping information

### `fulfillment`
Expands the fulfillment relation to include fulfillment details:
- Fulfillment number, status
- Tracking information
- Shipment dates

### `location`
Expands the location relation to include warehouse/store details:
- Location name, code
- Address information
- Location settings

### `items`
Expands the return_items relation to include all items in the return:
- Item quantities (requested, received, approved)
- Item condition and resalability
- Product and variant information
- Refund amounts per item

### `items.variant`
Nested expansion that includes return items with full variant details:
- All return item fields
- Complete variant object (SKU, title, price, etc.)

### `items.order_item`
Nested expansion that includes return items with original order item details:
- All return item fields
- Original order item data


## Common Use Cases

### 1. Get All Returns with Pagination

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 20
  }'
```

### 2. Get Pending Returns (Awaiting Approval)

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "status": "REQUESTED",
    "expand": "customer,order",
    "orderBy": "requested_at",
    "ascending": true
  }'
```

### 3. Get Returns for Specific Customer

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "customer": "customer-uuid-here",
    "expand": "order,items"
  }'
```

### 4. Get Returns for Specific Order

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "order": "order-uuid-here",
    "expand": "customer,items.variant"
  }'
```

### 5. Get Completed Returns Awaiting Refund

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "status": "COMPLETED",
    "refund_processed": false,
    "expand": "customer,order",
    "orderBy": "completed_at",
    "ascending": true
  }'
```

### 6. Get Returns in Transit

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "status": "IN_TRANSIT",
    "expand": "customer,order,location"
  }'
```

### 7. Search Returns by Number or Tracking

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "search": "RET-150000000001",
    "expand": "customer,order,items"
  }'
```

### 8. Get Returns by Date Range

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "requested_after": "2026-01-01",
    "requested_before": "2026-01-31",
    "expand": "customer,order"
  }'
```

### 9. Get Rejected Returns

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "status": "REJECTED",
    "expand": "customer,order",
    "orderBy": "rejected_at",
    "ascending": false
  }'
```

### 10. Get Returns by Reason

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3100/server/return/query \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "reason": "DEFECTIVE",
    "expand": "customer,order,items.variant"
  }'
```

